and one of the news items that continues  to percolate and eventually may  simmer and at some point may boil and  still could full out explode  is the relationship between the  pittsburgh steelers and ben  roethlisberger now a couple of weeks ago  we were led to believe that there would  be a middle ground there would be a  resolution there would be a new contract  a contract pursuant to which the  steelers would reduce the ben  roethlisberger cap number from 41.25  million  all the way down to 22.25  million that is a difference of  19 million dollars and no i didn't do  the math just then if i had i would have  gotten it wrong  so how do you save money under the cap  and keep ben roethlisberger it's a  simple proposition you take the 19  million he's due to make this year you  turn it into a signing bonus you extend  the contract by a few years with some  dummy years on the back end 22 23 24 and  you spread out that 19 million payment  we've done the numbers before it  wouldn't take much to put his cap number  in the range of say  26 million dollars  now the extra 15 million would hit the  cap in the future more specifically  would hit the cap next year but that's a  way to do it you can rob peter to pay  paul under the salary cap if you want to  keep ben roethlisberger and it felt like  that's the direction it was going art  rooney the owner of the team made it  clear they wanted him back for another  year and ben said hey i want to come  back and he also said i don't care how  much money i make well  well  now here we are and i got to give credit  to ed bouchette of the athletic he made  the point a couple of weeks ago that  even though both sides seem to be  willing to work this out  there's no guarantee they're going to  work it out and until they work it out  wait for it  it's not worked out  so kevin colbert the steelers gm  says  that  there isn't anything that has worked out  at this point and he didn't close the  door on the possibility that ben  roethlisberger won't be back and that  would happen if the steelers just decide  to take the 19 million dollar cap hit  that they're going to take this year  anyway whether he's on the team or not  they're taking a 19 million cap charge  for past money past contracts past  restructurings the question is how much  more do they want to commit to  rothsberger from a cash or cap  standpoint and they could decide that  whatever number they're willing to do  is less than what roethlisberger is  willing to take he can say i don't care  how much money i make you can say it  if they offer you a million dollars the  league minimum  and he says nah i care a little bit more  than that i don't care but i care a  little bit more than a million dollars  that's how it all falls apart and it  could be the steelers are deciding this  that now is the time to rip the band-aid  off that now's the time to move on you  know i haven't been a fan of this idea  that we're going to ride one more year  with ben roethlisberger understand the  attraction that's what they did with  jerome bettis in 2005. the year after  the steelers got close to the super bowl  15-1 ben roethlisberger's rookie season  thrust into action after tommy maddox  was injured i can still remember seeing  the quotes from alan fanuka new hall of  famer who wasn't sold on the idea of  having a rookie from the miami of ohio  come in and become the starting  quarterback well they did well well  enough to get bettis to believe next  year could end with a super bowl trophy  the problem is right now do you really  think steelers fans out there  do you really think  there's a good chance your team's going  to win the super bowl next year  with what the salary cap is going to do  to the team with the fact that key free  agents won't be back like juju smith  schuster and james connor and that other  guys like bud dupree he's coming off of  a touring acl are they going to keep him  around they're going to have to cut some  guys it's going to be a very different  team and i know that mike tomlin is very  good about taking the guys he has and  making them into something better than  what they are individually but even then  you compete with the chiefs  bills  ravens  browns  not so sure about that  and it could be that  the steelers just decide now is the time  to move on now is the time to turn the  page now is the time  to draft a new quarterback or let's see  what mason rudolph can do you know  not many people were paying attention to  the week 17 game between the browns and  the steelers because the steelers  weren't really trying but rudolph wasn't  bad in that game he was bad in 2019 but  he wasn't bad in that game and that was  a game the browns were trying to win to  punch their playoff ticket so they could  go to pittsburgh and punch the steelers  in the mouth the following week  either way the road is going to come to  an end for roethlisberger and i would  prefer  if i was a steelers fan i'll try to put  myself in the shoes of a steelers fan  i'd prefer let's just be done with it  now because there's a good chance that  when you get to the end of 2021 you're  going to regret  that you continued the relationship i  don't like one more year not in football  i don't want it i don't like it it just  needs to end and you can maybe think  it's your final year it's better to not  enter into it that way and i think  that's what the steelers may be finally  realizing and the other side of it too  is i don't think anybody wants to be the  villain in this  if it ends rothsberger wants it to be  the steelers fault if it ends the  steelers wanted to beat roethlisberger's  fault rothersberger wanted too much  money he said he'd take anything he  didn't take  anything that we offered he didn't want  to come back i just think they they both  and particularly the steelers would like  to find a way to to step back from this  and move on and understand that 2021 is  going to be  you know we we talk about rebuilding we  talk about reloading i think 2021 for  the steelers and i think this is the  first time i've ever used this in  context with a football team it's more  like regrouping  because  we don't know what they're going to have  whatever they have mike tomlin is going  to find a way to make it in a contender  and then you figure out this year who  are the guys that provide the nucleus  for 2022  and if you get lucky and you exceed all  expectations and you get to the playoffs  and win some games and somehow snake a  path to the super bowl so be it it's all  gravy but at some point  the gravy boat that is ben  roethlisberger's career needs to end and  it could be that now is the time to do  it  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

